00:45:49.480 --> 00:45:51.480
and how they have to worship him

00:45:51.480 --> 00:45:53.480
and how they do because they have been brainwashed

00:45:53.480 --> 00:45:56.480
and forced to believe, believe, believe their whole lives.

00:45:56.480 --> 00:45:58.480
And we over here do it voluntarily,

00:45:58.480 --> 00:46:01.480
and we do it because we don't ask questions.

00:46:01.480 --> 00:46:04.480
And so, what enemy, what enemy says,

00:46:04.480 --> 00:46:06.480
this is where I'm going to hit,

00:46:06.480 --> 00:46:08.480
and it's going to be not really you guys,

00:46:08.480 --> 00:46:10.480
but the territory that's far away from you guys.

00:46:10.480 --> 00:46:12.480
And so, none of this makes sense.

00:46:12.480 --> 00:46:15.480
In fact, if he launched, we would kill that missile

00:46:15.480 --> 00:46:16.480
in the air anyway.

00:46:16.480 --> 00:46:18.480
This is so preposterous and ridiculous,

00:46:18.480 --> 00:46:20.480
but Americans won't ask questions.

00:46:20.480 --> 00:46:22.480
They're so wrapped up in the emotion

00:46:22.480 --> 00:46:24.480
of the insults being going back and forth

00:46:24.480 --> 00:46:26.480
as top headline news.

00:46:26.480 --> 00:46:29.480
I posted something on Facebook today

00:46:29.480 --> 00:46:32.480
that was meant sort of tongue-in-cheek.

00:46:32.480 --> 00:46:34.480
It was one of these men on the street interviews

00:46:34.480 --> 00:46:38.480
where the reporter was asking random people,

00:46:38.480 --> 00:46:40.480
should we attack North Korea?

00:46:40.480 --> 00:46:42.480
And they all said yes.

00:46:42.480 --> 00:46:44.480
And then he shows them a map and says,

00:46:44.480 --> 00:46:46.480
can you tell me where North Korea is?

00:46:46.480 --> 00:46:48.480
And three of them pointed at Canada,

00:46:48.480 --> 00:46:51.480
two pointed to Finland.

00:46:51.480 --> 00:46:54.480
And this is so typical of the United States

00:46:54.480 --> 00:46:56.480
where we take these positions,

00:46:56.480 --> 00:46:58.480
and we don't have any idea what we're doing

00:46:58.480 --> 00:46:59.480
or what we're talking about.

00:46:59.480 --> 00:47:01.480
Yep. We're just taught to think a certain way.

00:47:01.480 --> 00:47:02.480
That's amazing.

00:47:02.480 --> 00:47:03.480
I agree with you completely.

00:47:03.480 --> 00:47:05.480
This is an utter lack of information,

00:47:05.480 --> 00:47:07.480
and even if we had the information,

00:47:07.480 --> 00:47:08.480
it's a lack of analysis.

00:47:08.480 --> 00:47:10.480
Yes. Yes.

00:47:10.480 --> 00:47:11.480
Oh, my gosh.

00:47:11.480 --> 00:47:13.480
I can't stress that enough.

00:47:13.480 --> 00:47:14.480
And what do you think will happen?

00:47:14.480 --> 00:47:16.480
What do you think will happen in the coming week?

00:47:16.480 --> 00:47:17.480
What do you foresee?

00:47:17.480 --> 00:47:18.480
I think we're serious.

00:47:18.480 --> 00:47:19.480
We're going to say these words,

00:47:19.480 --> 00:47:23.480
but I expect that the Chinese will finally

00:47:23.480 --> 00:47:25.480
intervene with both sides,

00:47:25.480 --> 00:47:26.480
and cooler heads will prevail.

00:47:26.480 --> 00:47:28.480
I can't believe that we're looking to the Chinese

00:47:28.480 --> 00:47:29.480
for leadership.

00:47:29.480 --> 00:47:30.480
But here we are.

00:47:30.480 --> 00:47:31.480
Wow.

00:47:31.480 --> 00:47:32.480
We live in a bizarro world now.

00:47:32.480 --> 00:47:33.480
Wow.

00:47:33.480 --> 00:47:34.480
A false flag.

00:47:34.480 --> 00:47:37.480
How do you feel about those words?

00:47:37.480 --> 00:47:41.480
You know, it depends, really.

00:47:41.480 --> 00:47:43.480
False flags were actually very popular

00:47:43.480 --> 00:47:45.480
at the CIA when I was there.

00:47:45.480 --> 00:47:46.480
Not on grand scales,

00:47:46.480 --> 00:47:48.480
because the bigger the false flag,

00:47:48.480 --> 00:47:50.480
the tougher it is to pull it off.

00:47:50.480 --> 00:47:54.480
But operationally, false flags were very popular.

00:47:54.480 --> 00:47:56.480
They used them all the time.

00:47:56.480 --> 00:47:59.480
I'm glad you at least commented on that.

00:47:59.480 --> 00:48:01.480
You know, those words are so taboo.

00:48:01.480 --> 00:48:02.480
Very good.

00:48:02.480 --> 00:48:05.480
They are, you know, because they're loaded.

00:48:05.480 --> 00:48:08.480
For example, I don't believe that the new town

00:48:08.480 --> 00:48:09.480
massacre was a false flag.

00:48:09.480 --> 00:48:12.480
I think it was a massacre.

00:48:12.480 --> 00:48:16.480
And it's funny to me that I have so many friends

00:48:16.480 --> 00:48:19.480
who believe that everything is a false flag.

00:48:19.480 --> 00:48:21.480
And it's like, dude, you know,

00:48:21.480 --> 00:48:22.480
I want to tell people,

00:48:22.480 --> 00:48:23.480
if you knew the morons,

00:48:23.480 --> 00:48:26.480
some of the morons I worked with at the CIA,

00:48:26.480 --> 00:48:28.480
you would never use the words false flags again,

00:48:28.480 --> 00:48:30.480
because these guys can't find their way to the men's room,

00:48:30.480 --> 00:48:33.480
let alone manipulate governments and countries.

00:48:33.480 --> 00:48:34.480
Interesting.

00:48:34.480 --> 00:48:37.480
What is your take on Russia and the allegations

00:48:37.480 --> 00:48:38.480
with Trump and Russia?

00:48:38.480 --> 00:48:39.480
Because I don't believe it for a second.

00:48:39.480 --> 00:48:40.480
But what do you...

00:48:40.480 --> 00:48:42.480
I actually don't believe it for a second either.

00:48:42.480 --> 00:48:44.480
I'm a member of a group called

00:48:44.480 --> 00:48:46.480
Veteran Intelligence Professionals for Sanity.

00:48:46.480 --> 00:48:50.480
We've got about five dozen former CIA,

00:48:50.480 --> 00:48:55.480
FBI and NSA, mostly senior officials.

00:48:55.480 --> 00:48:57.480
In some cases, you know, the number two

00:48:57.480 --> 00:48:59.480
or the number three or number four in some of these agencies.

00:48:59.480 --> 00:49:02.480
And we take very in-depth looks

00:49:02.480 --> 00:49:04.480
at some of these major issues,

00:49:04.480 --> 00:49:07.480
and then we issue memoranda to the president,

00:49:07.480 --> 00:49:09.480
which he probably never reads,

00:49:09.480 --> 00:49:11.480
but they also get published in places

00:49:11.480 --> 00:49:13.480
like Consortium News or The Nation Magazine.

00:49:13.480 --> 00:49:15.480
And we wrote one a few days ago

00:49:15.480 --> 00:49:17.480
on this Russia collusion thing.

00:49:17.480 --> 00:49:19.480
It was written by Bill Benny,

00:49:19.480 --> 00:49:21.480
who was the number four at NSA

00:49:21.480 --> 00:49:24.480
and is one of the country's leading experts

00:49:24.480 --> 00:49:26.480
on internet security.

00:49:26.480 --> 00:49:28.480
And we've come to the conclusion

00:49:28.480 --> 00:49:33.480
that there is just no evidence of collusion.

00:49:33.480 --> 00:49:35.480
There's no evidence that the Russians

00:49:35.480 --> 00:49:38.480
hacked into the DNC servers.

00:49:38.480 --> 00:49:41.480
The evidence that we do have points to

00:49:41.480 --> 00:49:43.480
a whistleblower inside the DNC

00:49:43.480 --> 00:49:45.480
who printed the documents off,

00:49:45.480 --> 00:49:48.480
gave them to the former British ambassador

00:49:48.480 --> 00:49:50.480
to Uzbekistan, Craig Murray.

00:49:50.480 --> 00:49:52.480
And Craig delivered them to WikiLeaks.

00:49:52.480 --> 00:49:54.480
And Craig has said publicly

00:49:54.480 --> 00:49:56.480
that that's exactly what happened.

00:49:56.480 --> 00:49:59.480
So I'm just not seeing any collusion.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:02.520
between the Trump campaign and the Russians.

00:50:02.520 --> 00:50:03.600
I just don't think it's there.

00:50:03.600 --> 00:50:05.520
I think the Paul Manafort thing was all,

00:50:05.520 --> 00:50:09.400
I don't like him, but it was all theater, theater, yeah.

00:50:09.400 --> 00:50:12.000
Yeah, it's all theater.

00:50:12.000 --> 00:50:14.160
You know, John Stockwell, the CIA agent

00:50:14.160 --> 00:50:15.360
that came out in the 80s,

00:50:15.360 --> 00:50:16.840
said something that I'll never forget,

00:50:16.840 --> 00:50:19.560
and I've regurgitated it a couple times on the show,

00:50:19.560 --> 00:50:22.040
that he was always, when he was told to do things,

00:50:22.040 --> 00:50:23.960
he always thought that he would get the answer

00:50:23.960 --> 00:50:26.720
as to why, and as long as he kept moving up

00:50:26.720 --> 00:50:27.880
the food chain, and then when he got

00:50:27.880 --> 00:50:28.920
to the top of the food chain,

00:50:28.920 --> 00:50:30.080
he was never given answers.

00:50:30.080 --> 00:50:31.880
It was all smoke and mirrors.

00:50:31.880 --> 00:50:33.720
What are your thoughts on that, being in the CIA?

00:50:33.720 --> 00:50:37.440
I think that's absolutely true, absolutely true.

00:50:37.440 --> 00:50:40.040
You know, when I got this job as the executive assistant

00:50:40.040 --> 00:50:43.640
to the ADDO, the associate deputy director for operations,

00:50:44.760 --> 00:50:47.600
I mean, that's a pretty doggone, high level position.

00:50:47.600 --> 00:50:49.840
In that, even though I'm the assistant,

00:50:49.840 --> 00:50:53.480
I then have access to, I thought, literally everything.

00:50:53.480 --> 00:50:54.640
Right.

00:50:54.640 --> 00:50:55.640
Because that's the only way

00:50:55.640 --> 00:50:58.680
that I can keep him briefed or informed.

00:50:58.680 --> 00:51:02.240
Well, there were databases that I had access to

00:51:02.240 --> 00:51:05.000
called Compartmented Databases,

00:51:05.000 --> 00:51:07.680
and I remember a couple of times like starting

00:51:07.680 --> 00:51:09.240
to brief something that I had read

00:51:09.240 --> 00:51:12.840
from one of these databases, and he stopped me

00:51:12.840 --> 00:51:16.000
because the other associate deputy directors

00:51:16.000 --> 00:51:18.060
didn't have access to the information.

00:51:19.120 --> 00:51:21.760
And so I would have to give it to him hard copy,

00:51:21.760 --> 00:51:23.640
and he said, you know, you can't mention this

00:51:23.640 --> 00:51:24.600
in front of anybody else.

00:51:24.600 --> 00:51:26.200
Oh my God, these are the top,

00:51:26.200 --> 00:51:27.880
top most people in the CIA.

00:51:27.880 --> 00:51:28.840
Right.

00:51:28.840 --> 00:51:30.680
And they're not cleared for the information.

00:51:30.680 --> 00:51:33.000
So it was that that made me understand that,

00:51:33.000 --> 00:51:36.160
oh, this went way higher than I had ever thought.

00:51:36.160 --> 00:51:37.000
Right.

00:51:37.000 --> 00:51:39.280
I mean, it went above the CIA even.

00:51:39.280 --> 00:51:41.280
I mean, look at Richard Helms, for example,

00:51:41.280 --> 00:51:43.480
the former CIA director,

00:51:43.480 --> 00:51:45.920
who went fishing one day,

00:51:45.920 --> 00:51:48.560
and then mysteriously died in his canoe

00:51:48.560 --> 00:51:51.320
all by himself and fell overboard and drowned.

00:51:51.320 --> 00:51:52.440
I mean, how does that happen?

00:51:52.440 --> 00:51:54.580
Well, don't you worry about that?

00:51:54.580 --> 00:51:56.860
I mean, John Stockwell, I think he's still alive.

00:51:56.860 --> 00:51:58.020
Don't you worry about that?

00:51:58.020 --> 00:51:59.820
Don't you worry about saying things

00:51:59.820 --> 00:52:01.900
that I mean, a lot of people turn up dead,

00:52:01.900 --> 00:52:03.260
especially if you know the Clintons

00:52:03.260 --> 00:52:05.020
or pass the Clintons in traffic

00:52:05.020 --> 00:52:07.300
or brush up against them in a hotel or whatever.

00:52:07.300 --> 00:52:09.700
Lots of people around the Clintons die.

00:52:09.700 --> 00:52:11.860
Don't you worry about that in this position?

00:52:11.860 --> 00:52:14.300
Because whistleblowers are right out there,

00:52:14.300 --> 00:52:15.340
you know, in the open.

00:52:15.340 --> 00:52:16.900
They are.

00:52:16.900 --> 00:52:17.740
Do you worry?

00:52:17.740 --> 00:52:18.980
People ask me that all the time,

00:52:18.980 --> 00:52:21.140
and to tell you the honest to God's truth,

00:52:21.140 --> 00:52:23.500
yeah, I am a little bit worried about it,

00:52:23.540 --> 00:52:28.540
but I like to think that if I remain as vocal

00:52:28.780 --> 00:52:31.620
and as out there as I possibly can be,

00:52:31.620 --> 00:52:34.780
shouting the truth, that people will miss me.

00:52:36.300 --> 00:52:39.180
And I like to think that that's what keeps me safe.

00:52:39.180 --> 00:52:40.820
Wow.

00:52:40.820 --> 00:52:41.660
Wow.

00:52:41.660 --> 00:52:42.500
I have a question.

00:52:42.500 --> 00:52:43.340
Sure.

00:52:43.340 --> 00:52:44.340
Since you were talking about torture,

00:52:44.340 --> 00:52:45.500
are we still doing it?

00:52:47.180 --> 00:52:48.020
The wink and the nod.

00:52:48.020 --> 00:52:50.300
Oh, that's another good question.

00:52:50.300 --> 00:52:53.420
You know, Barack Obama said that we weren't.

00:52:53.420 --> 00:52:54.260
I believe him.

00:52:54.260 --> 00:52:55.220
I believe everything he says.

00:52:55.220 --> 00:52:56.860
Who knows?

00:52:56.860 --> 00:52:58.140
It's all secret.

00:52:58.140 --> 00:52:59.340
Right.

00:52:59.340 --> 00:53:00.380
Right.

00:53:00.380 --> 00:53:01.220
Because I believe it.

00:53:01.220 --> 00:53:03.180
I told an interview with the other day

00:53:03.180 --> 00:53:06.540
that when the CIA told the American people

00:53:06.540 --> 00:53:09.260
that there was no torture program, that was a lie.

00:53:09.260 --> 00:53:11.860
When they said that there were no secret prisons,

00:53:11.860 --> 00:53:13.140
that was a lie.

00:53:13.140 --> 00:53:16.300
When they said that they were not rendering prisoners

00:53:16.300 --> 00:53:18.420
to third countries, that was a lie.

00:53:18.420 --> 00:53:20.060
When they say that they had not

00:53:20.060 --> 00:53:22.500
hacked into the Senate's computer system,

00:53:22.540 --> 00:53:23.980
that was a lie.

00:53:23.980 --> 00:53:26.300
So why should we take their word for it now?

00:53:26.300 --> 00:53:27.140
I totally agree with you.

00:53:27.140 --> 00:53:29.460
With everything else that they've told us has been a lie.

00:53:29.460 --> 00:53:30.300
Yep.

00:53:30.300 --> 00:53:31.340
I totally agree with you.

00:53:31.340 --> 00:53:33.020
I wish people would follow the dots on that.

00:53:33.020 --> 00:53:35.260
And how do you feel about the CMUs,

00:53:35.260 --> 00:53:36.700
the secret management units,

00:53:36.700 --> 00:53:38.380
the communication management units

00:53:38.380 --> 00:53:39.860
where people are completely denied

00:53:39.860 --> 00:53:42.020
of all their rights if they're a political prisoner?

00:53:42.020 --> 00:53:44.180
They're located in, I think, Indiana, Illinois?

00:53:44.180 --> 00:53:47.300
I was threatened with placement in a CMU.

00:53:47.300 --> 00:53:50.700
When I started writing this block series from prison

00:53:50.700 --> 00:53:53.420
that became the book, Doing Time Like a Spy.

00:53:54.540 --> 00:53:57.380
So they threatened me with transfer to another prison

00:53:57.380 --> 00:53:58.980
and placement in the CMU.

00:53:58.980 --> 00:53:59.820
Oh my gosh.

00:53:59.820 --> 00:54:00.940
The management unit.

00:54:00.940 --> 00:54:01.780
Right.

00:54:01.780 --> 00:54:03.460
Communications management unit.

00:54:03.460 --> 00:54:05.940
And I decided to use a little bit of bluster.

00:54:05.940 --> 00:54:09.380
And I told the warden right to his face.

00:54:09.380 --> 00:54:11.700
He stopped me coming out of the cafeteria

00:54:11.700 --> 00:54:13.540
at lunch one day to threaten me.

00:54:13.540 --> 00:54:16.340
And I said, warden, I have gone nose to nose

00:54:16.340 --> 00:54:20.660
with Al Qaeda, with Hezbollah, with the Iranians,

00:54:20.700 --> 00:54:23.540
and I'm supposed to be afraid of your prisons?

00:54:23.540 --> 00:54:26.660
Please, I said, give me a little bit of credit.

00:54:26.660 --> 00:54:30.220
My sentence is short, and I'm gonna go home,

00:54:30.220 --> 00:54:31.780
and I'm gonna tell the American people

00:54:31.780 --> 00:54:33.860
what happens inside these prisons.

00:54:33.860 --> 00:54:35.660
You can't scare me into silence.

00:54:36.780 --> 00:54:38.260
Whoa.

00:54:38.260 --> 00:54:40.220
You know, I, yeah.

00:54:40.220 --> 00:54:43.060
I fear, wow.

00:54:43.060 --> 00:54:45.580
I fear that Congress oversees this,

00:54:45.580 --> 00:54:47.660
but they don't do anything about it.

00:54:47.660 --> 00:54:50.540
We see these things, they'll never, ever go away.

00:54:50.540 --> 00:54:55.100
And they're so, it's like a little mini Guantanamo, really,

00:54:55.100 --> 00:54:56.740
because they could be put in a hole.

00:54:56.740 --> 00:54:57.740
People could be put in a hole.

00:54:57.740 --> 00:54:59.460
These are people that really haven't harmed anyone.

00:54:59.460 --> 00:55:01.900
This is just mostly a lot of political prisoners.

00:55:01.900 --> 00:55:05.460
And so they could be put in a hole, and you wouldn't know.

00:55:05.460 --> 00:55:07.100
And they could be stuck down there for 25 years.

00:55:07.100 --> 00:55:08.980
There's no accountability, border prisons,

00:55:08.980 --> 00:55:10.780
no accountability whatsoever.

00:55:10.780 --> 00:55:12.180
Why does that not get out?

00:55:12.180 --> 00:55:13.660
Why doesn't that worry Americans

00:55:13.660 --> 00:55:16.340
that we have this right here in good old USA?

00:55:16.340 --> 00:55:18.340
You are absolutely right.

00:55:18.340 --> 00:55:19.900
And in the federal prison system,

00:55:19.900 --> 00:55:23.260
they use this technique called diesel therapy.

00:55:23.260 --> 00:55:24.860
I was threatened with diesel therapy

00:55:24.860 --> 00:55:27.060
and a friendly administrator warned me.

00:55:27.060 --> 00:55:28.220
He said, hey, they're talking about

00:55:28.220 --> 00:55:29.340
putting you in diesel therapy.

00:55:29.340 --> 00:55:30.260
I said, what's that mean?

00:55:30.260 --> 00:55:31.780
I had never heard it before.

00:55:31.780 --> 00:55:33.820
What it means is, they put you in something

00:55:33.820 --> 00:55:35.500
called transit status.

00:55:35.500 --> 00:55:38.140
That's that you're being transferred to another prison.

00:55:38.140 --> 00:55:39.460
So I would go from,

00:55:39.460 --> 00:55:42.380
I was in the federal prison at Laredo, Pennsylvania.

00:55:42.380 --> 00:55:44.820
They would send me to the US Penitentiary

00:55:44.820 --> 00:55:46.260
in Canaan, Pennsylvania.

00:55:46.260 --> 00:55:48.180
And I'm there for three days or three weeks

00:55:48.180 --> 00:55:49.620
or three months or whatever.

00:55:49.620 --> 00:55:51.780
And then from there, they'd send me to Atlanta

00:55:51.780 --> 00:55:53.380
and from Atlanta to Oklahoma City,

00:55:53.380 --> 00:55:55.260
which is the National Transportation Hub

00:55:55.260 --> 00:55:57.140
and from Oklahoma City to another place

00:55:57.140 --> 00:55:58.500
and another and another.

00:55:58.500 --> 00:56:03.020
With the idea being, if you are in transit status,

00:56:03.020 --> 00:56:06.180
you're not allowed to have access to a phone,

00:56:06.180 --> 00:56:09.420
to an email system or to pen and paper.

00:56:09.420 --> 00:56:10.260
Zip.

00:56:10.260 --> 00:56:13.140
And so people literally have no idea

00:56:13.140 --> 00:56:15.340
where you are in the country.

00:56:15.340 --> 00:56:16.180
Oh.

00:56:16.180 --> 00:56:17.620
And you can't contact anybody.

00:56:17.620 --> 00:56:18.940
It's amazing.

00:56:18.940 --> 00:56:20.260
And I want, just before we go,

00:56:20.260 --> 00:56:21.420
we have about a minute and a half.

